{
	quest.042DA7EF2501C94E.quest_desc: [
		"&6ME Chest&r is essentially an &eME Terminal&r and a &eME Drive&r combined! They only accept &bone storage cell at a time&r however. This is good for when you want to see what is exactly inside of a specific storage cell."
		""
		"You can insert storage cells by clicking the ME Chest on the side and then access the storage cell by clicking the top of the ME Chest."
	]
	quest.096E1D8BBDE19DFE.quest_desc: ["Next up is getting &6Fluix Crystals&r. You can make Fluix Crystals by throwing &eCharged Quartz&r, &eNether Quartz&r and &eRedstone Dust&r into water. After a while, those materials will be turned into Fluix Crystals."]
	quest.096E1D8BBDE19DFE.quest_subtitle: "Fluix Soup"
	quest.096E1D8BBDE19DFE.title: "Getting Fluix Crystal"
	quest.0B5C65B4C0EDFB95.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystal Resonance Generators&r generate AE for absolutely free! However, there ever can &4&l<pulse>only be one Crystal Resonance Generator per network</pulse>&r."
		""
		"They are enough to power a VERY SIMPLE storage network, one that is made out of only a &eTerminal&r and either a &eME Drive&r or &eStorage Bus&r."
	]
	quest.0BD71C3D52DB1DB4.quest_desc: [
		"Any other block that isn't covered here might be too advanced for a player that's using AE2 for the first time or hasn't experienced a lot of advanced tech mods."
		""
		"Blocks that use any of the materials required on this quest indicate that they're more advanced topic."
	]
	quest.0BD71C3D52DB1DB4.title: "Advanced Stuff"
	quest.14BE11EB87E5D2E8.quest_desc: [
		"Since you're able to upgrade a regular &eTerminal&r into a &eCrafting Terminal&r, you should be able to do the same with a &eWireless Terminal&r, right?"
		""
		"Well you can! Now you're able to craft anywhere you please!!! &0&oHuh, wait you could already do that...&r&r"
	]
	quest.14BE11EB87E5D2E8.quest_subtitle: "Get Crafting anywhere you go! Hold up."
	quest.14BE11EB87E5D2E8.title: "Wireless Crafting"
	quest.1889D7C75371138D.quest_desc: [
		"To access any of your items that are connected to your network, you will need an &6ME Terminal&r. Simply place it on top of a cable and you can then open up a menu where you can take and insert items out or into of."
		""
		"Keep in mind that taking and inserting items also drains power from your network! If you notice that you can't insert or take out a full stack, that might be why."
		""
		"<rainb>Fun Fact</rainb>"
		"The color of the terminal is determined by the cable it is placed on!"
	]
	quest.22D647D9775EE4FB.quest_desc: [
		"&oDo you find it annoying always having to go to a point to access your items? Or maybe you're tired of putting terminals all over your base? Wish you could access your network anywhere around your base?&r"
		"If you said &aYES&r to any of these questions, then I have the answer for you: <rainb w=-1><wave a=0.25>WIRELESS</wave></rainb>"
		""
		"Simply craft an &6ME Wireless Access Point&r and a &6Wireless Terminal&r and you'll be able to just do that! Place the Access Point anywhere on your network and then link the Terminal inside of the Access Point's GUI in the top right slot."
		""
		"Make sure that you're generating enough power to sustain the Access Point and that your Terminal is charged. You can charge your Terminal just like how you'd charge &eNether Quartz&r into &eCharged Quartz&r."
		""
		"If you've done everything correctly, you will be able to &baccess your items by right clicking the Terminal&r! You can also open the Terminal by binding a keybind!"
	]
	quest.22D647D9775EE4FB.title: "Wireless Technology"
	quest.257A9CF3C232A9F9.quest_desc: [
		"A network can only have up to 8 channels. This is a very low amount even if you don't go for any advanced setups."
		""
		"If you want to increase the number, you will need to get an &6ME Controller&r. A single ME Controller will give you &b32 channels &9PER SIDE!&r That way you can connect more &eME Drives&r or more &eStorage Buses&r to your network."
		""
		"The ME Controller also allows you to see how much power your network consumes."
		""
		"You can connect multiple ME Controller together to get even more channel, but they have certain placement rules:"
		"&o&l  1. You can only have one ME Controller per network&r"
		"&o&l  2. The biggest ME Controller you can build is 7x7x7&r"
		"&o&l  3. There can only be up to two ME Controllers connected to another ME Controller on each axis&r"
		"If these are hard to visualize, I recommend to open the guide page by holding G on an ME Controller. &8<wave a=0.2>You can even do it on the one in this quest.</wave>&r"
	]
	quest.271BBFEB9B1542C2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Cables&r are a way to connect your components together to form a network. A lot of AE2 blocks are able to connect together even without cables, such as &eME Drives&r."
		""
		"&6Channels&r are an important aspect in AE2, which simply limits how many components you can connect together in a single network. Each machine always takes up a channel."
		""
		"Fluix ME Glass Cables are able to transfer 8 channels."
		""
		"The difference between Quartz Fiber and Fluix ME Glass Cables is that &bQuartz Fiber only transfers power across&r them, while &bFluix ME Glass Cables transfer both power and channels across&r. Thus Quartz Fiber allows you to create \"sub-networks\" inside of your networks, but that's a more advanced topic in the mod, so you can, for the most part, just use Fluix ME Glass Cables."
	]
	quest.271BBFEB9B1542C2.title: "Cables \\& Channels"
	quest.298309CB9C818953.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Quantum Ring&r is special multiblock structure, that allows you to setup your network in another location without routing a bunch of cables all over the world. Even across dimensions!"
		""
		"You normally need two of them that you then link together, but in this case you only need one!"
		"Simply build a square using the 8 &6ME Quantum Rings&r and place the &6ME Quantum Link Chamber&r in the middle anywhere on your network."
		""
		"If they change appearance, then you have built the Quantum Ring correctly and you may proceed to the next quest!"
		""
		"Make sure you increase the amount of power you're generating before you attach a Quantum Ring to your network! These things cost &c&l<turb>A LOT</turb>&r of power to run."
	]
	quest.298309CB9C818953.title: "Quantum Ring"
	quest.29A82FBB4DB8D707.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Quartz Wrench&r allows you to rotate an AE2 block with right click or disassemble it with sneak and right click."
		""
		"Did you know you can also use a &eCreate Wrench&r for the exact same purpose?"
	]
	quest.2F9425B2FD068546.quest_desc: [
		"You probably noticed that the base range for wireless access is relatively small. Well, you're able to fix it by crafting &6Wireless Boosters&r! Add up to 64 of them inside of an &eAccess Point&r and you'll increase the range you can access your network with your &eTerminal&r."
		""
		"&cAdding Wireless Boosters will increase your networks power consumption.&r"
	]
	quest.39CDD4C0E2386618.quest_desc: [
		"Some of these materials will be needed for AE2. Make sure to gather these before starting!"
		""
		"You probably won't use all of the materials listed here and will end up with excess, but it's better to have more than enough than to end up with one missing item."
	]
	quest.39CDD4C0E2386618.title: "Gather some materials"
	quest.3A831A10A3B9755C.quest_desc: ["&6Smart Cables&r have a display on them that visualizes &bhow many channels are transfered&r through the cable and through &eJade&r (the tooltip that appears at the top of your screen when you're looking at something)."]
	quest.3DFE204F74CCE7F2.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to use your &echests&r or &eitem vaults&r as part of your storage network, you can craft a &6ME Storage Bus&r. Just attach it to whatever container you want to use and connect the bus to your network and your network will have access to those items!"
		""
		"Here's a simple physical storage setup using a &eCrystal Resonance Generator&r and Create's &eItem Vaults&r."
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/storage/physical.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3DFE204F74CCE7F2.title: "Physical Storage"
	quest.40809A14D402451D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluix ME Covered Cables&r are not really much different between the regular &eFluix ME Glass Cables&r, other than asthetics."
		""
		"&6Fluix ME Dense Covered Cable&r, however, are able to carry &b32 channels&r instead of only 8 of their smaller counterpart!"
	]
	quest.40809A14D402451D.title: "Covered Cables"
	quest.4738D378459007A4.quest_desc: ["Want to be able to also craft at the same time you're viewing your items? Upgrade your &eME Terminal&r into a &6ME Crafting Terminal&r, that contains a crafting table!"]
	quest.4AC31490A94B6B22.quest_desc: [
		"Normally, AE2 blocks don't accept any energy from other mods, one of these exceptions being the &6Charger&r."
		""
		"This is where the &6Energy Acceptor&r comes in. It converts any energy pushed into it into AE, that then can be used by AE2 blocks."
		""
		"&8&oYes, the energy in Applied Energistics 2 is called AE.&r&r"
	]
	quest.4AC31490A94B6B22.quest_subtitle: "AE2 uses AE"
	quest.4AC31490A94B6B22.title: "Energy Acceptor"
	quest.4B1E8E7E067BD2A0.quest_desc: [
		"To create &6Singularities&r, you will need to condense A LOT of matter. To do so, you will need a &6Matter Condenser&r."
		""
		"You will also need a &6256k ME Storage Components&r so that the Matter Condenser is even able to store the amount of matter to condense into a Singularity. To confirm your suspicion, yes, you will &bneed 256000 of any item or liquid to compress into a Singularity&r. So you better have a lot of trash lying around or a really good Cobblestone generator. An infinite water source also works!"
		""
		"The good thing is that the Matter Condenser doesn't need power, so you only need to worry about the mass amount of things you want to void!"
	]
	quest.4B1E8E7E067BD2A0.title: "Creating singularities"
	quest.5057F515A406781E.quest_desc: [
		"By now, you should have the &eQuantum Bridge Card&r, two &eEntangled Singularities&r and a &eQuantum Ring&r built on your network."
		""
		"Make sure you have also increased the amount of power you're generating! &c<shake>Quantum Rings are power-hungry!!!</shake>"
		""
		"Now all that's left to do is to &binsert one of the Entangled Singularities into the Quantum Ring&r. Afterwards, &bopen your Wireless &lCRAFTING&r&b Terminal and insert the Quantum Bridge Card&r at the top right, &bfollowed by the other Entangled Singularity&r."
		""
		"And you're done! If you've done everything right, you should have wireless access anywhere in any dimension. Be sure that you still have a &eWireless Access Point&r somewhere in your network, that your &eTerminal&r is linked to. You can remove the &eWireless Boosters&r if you want though."
	]
	quest.5057F515A406781E.title: "Putting it all together"
	quest.5551433207866F92.quest_desc: [
		"One of the main materials is &6Charged Quartz&r. You can get it by, well, &bcharging Nether Quartz&r."
		""
		"You can do this with a &6Charger&r. You can power the Charger by either using &eany of the AE2 generators&r, &eany other generators from other mods&r or ,if you're really poor, with a &6Wooden Crank&r. Just slap it on the Charger and right click to crank it!"
		""
		"&8<wiggle a=0.3>The crank is really fragile though and might break after a while...</wiggle>&r"
	]
	quest.5551433207866F92.quest_subtitle: "POOOWEEER!!!!"
	quest.5551433207866F92.title: "Getting Charged Quartz"
	quest.580B63D793639AC0.quest_desc: [
		"You can dye the cables any of the vanilla dye colors, even the &eDense&r and &eSmart cables&r!"
		""
		"Not only will they allow you to identify cables better if you're running multiple, but they also won't connect with each other unless they're the undyed regular &eFluix Cables&r."
		""
		"Make sure you don't confuse the undyed cables with the purple ones though, <shake a=0.3>they look very alike...</shake>"
		""
		""
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/storage/cables.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.580B63D793639AC0.quest_subtitle: "<rainb>TASTE THE RAINBOW!</rainb>"
	quest.5A6FE5CB450BC0FD.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Network Tool&r is a slightly more advanced &eQuartz Wrench&r."
		""
		"Right clicking on your network will open up a window that shows you information, such as how much power is being generated and consumed."
		""
		"It also allows you to store upgrade cards."
	]
	quest.5CFDE37DACC8D41C.quest_desc: [
		"By now you might be wishing that you could access your storage ANYWHERE, including in other dimensions."
		""
		"It's possible, BUT requires a bit more setup to get it started."
		"You will need to"
		"  1. Get a &ewireless card&r"
		"  2. Split a &esingularity&r into two &eentangled singularities&r"
		"  3. Setup a &equantum ring&r on your network"
		""
		"Probably sounds complicated, but do not worry! The next quests will explain how you can get to that point."
	]
	quest.5CFDE37DACC8D41C.title: "The road to TRUE wireless"
	quest.60BD1FEEF411CDB2.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have a &eSingularity&r, you will need to split it into two &6Quantum Entangled Singularities&r. How do you manage such a feat? It's quite simple honestly; &bblowing up a Singularity and en Ender Pearl&r."
		""
		"A &eTNT&r explosion will do just fine! Hell, even a &etiny TNT&r explosion is enough."
		"&oNot a Creeper explosion though... Don't try to cheap your way out of this!&r"
	]
	quest.60BD1FEEF411CDB2.title: "Splitting singularities"
	quest.6640C7E29137C1D0.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Energistics 2 also comes bundles with a guide book that you can access at any time!"
		""
		"You can either get yourself an &6Guide&r or you can just press &6G&r &8(default keybind)&r on any AE2 item to get its page, similar to &eCreate's Ponder system&r."
	]
	quest.6640C7E29137C1D0.quest_subtitle: "Like Create but not"
	quest.6640C7E29137C1D0.title: "Guide Book"
	quest.677B8E00B6DC2A55.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Energistics 2 allows you to store items digitally! You need an &6ME Drive&r where you can store your &6storage cells&r. You can move the storage cells, even when they already have items inside of them."
		""
		"Be warned though that the only way to interact with the items inside of a storage cell is either through &eME Terminals&r or an &eME Chests&r! &cIf you have no way to power any of those, then you won't be able to access any of your items.&r"
		""
		"Here's a simple digital storage setup using a &eCrystal Resonance Generator&r."
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/storage/digital.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"Storage cells come in &b1k&r, &b4k&r, &b16k&r, &b64k&r and &b256k&r variants. Although they increase how many items they can hold, they do NOT increase the amount of item types they can hold."
		""
		"&6Item types&r are simply how many unique items are inside of the cell. You can &bimagine them similar to how a slot works in a chest&r. You can add items into a chest if you have free slots available or if any other slot already has the exact same item stored inside of them. "
		""
		"This is why it's a &cbad idea to hook your AE2 network to a farm without any filtering&r, because those mobs may drop equipment, which all have different durability, and, therefore, will each take a different item type."
	]
	quest.677B8E00B6DC2A55.quest_subtitle: "(and item types)"
	quest.677B8E00B6DC2A55.title: "Digital Storage"
	quest.686DC1A54331B658.quest_desc: ["&6Energy Cells&r are basically just batteries. It's good to have a few in your network to make sure that when your power generation shuts off or you're doing an expensive task on your system, your network will still be able to run for a while, so you aren't locked off from accessing your items."]
	quest.698EEC6AC7E52E01.quest_desc: ["The &6Stock Bridge&r is an useful block to connect your AE2 storage network with your Create storage network."]
	quest.6D886AAEA5519E75.quest_desc: ["This card doesn't do anything on its own..."]
	quest.6F43C19FAEA40F69.quest_desc: ["A &6Vibration Chamber&r is a simple generator that takes any fuel item and burns them into AE."]
	quest.7658FF17537C7F35.quest_desc: [
		"If you ever want to run your cables through your floor or walls, or you just want to hide them in general, you can do that with &6Cable Facades&r!"
		""
		"You can make Facades pretty much out of any block, using the block and &6Cable Anchors&r. You then can attach the Facades on any side of a cable or even &eTerminal&r!"
		""
		"Cable Anchors are made using a &6Cutting Knife&r and a metal ingot. They too can be placed on cables, which stops the cable from connecting to any other cable on that side!"
	]
	quest.7658FF17537C7F35.title: "Anchors and Cable Facades"
	quest.7FF215B35ECD8147.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Energistics 2 has received several recipe changes in this pack to make the items of the mod easier to obtain for players who haven't really touched AE2."
		""
		"It's meant to be a &ereplacement for Tom's Simple Storage&r, as that mod can be quite laggy, especially on servers. Therefore, the recipes have been simplified to somewhat match the recipes from TSS."
		""
		"These quests will try to attempt to guide a novice player in setting up an AE2 system that they can use for storage. &bAny feedback on these quests is welcome!&r"
		""
		"Blocks and items that aren't meant for storage, &esuch as autocrafting&r, are still available, but haven't received any simplified recipes. This is to indicate inexperienced players that those components &emight be too advanced for them&r. Those won't also be covered in these quests and it is recommended for players to look up tutorials instead, if they want to learn advanced AE2 applications that isn't just storage."
		""
		"&c&l&nFor advanced players&r&r&r"
		"Meteors have been disabled and do not spawn. Presses and several other materials aren't needed to progress through AE2. The materials have been simplified to mostly just Charged Quartz and Fluix Crystals. Inscribers have also been disabled and the components made using them are made with Create machines instead."
	]
	quest.7FF215B35ECD8147.quest_subtitle: "Applied Energistics 2 has received some big changes in this pack!"
	quest.7FF215B35ECD8147.title: "Before we begin"
	task.0601A6F4D885FFFC.title: "I understand"
	task.060B4E03962EE051.title: "Cable Facade"
	task.0DC590BC0E6ABE76.title: "Smart Cable"
	task.107A27E1A97AE35B.title: "Covered Cable"
	task.2278C429F1A0A1AA.title: "I want complete wireless access!"
	task.23414548209E3ED1.title: "Cutting Knife"
	task.24CCE26CE0B88E2F.title: "Quartz Wrench"
	task.429E6D13606070A2.title: "Energy Cell"
	task.489DF1072DB4CF37.title: "Any dye"
	task.6DC7A9BE1F978D32.title: "Energy Acceptor"
}
